# Logs
logs
*.log
# EXCEPT reviewer evidence: item artifacts are REQUIRED in the committed record - the codex-lane
# stderr log carries the run header (model and effort pins, vendor session id), the only key that
# attributes reviewer spend to an item. The blanket *.log rule was silently fighting that
# requirement and every evidence commit needed a force-add (founder ruling 2026-08-12: fix it).
!loop/items/**/artifacts/*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
.output
.vinxi
.tanstack/**
.nitro
*.local

# Wrangler / Cloudflare
.wrangler/
.dev.vars

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Local environment overrides — secrets live here, never in the tracked .env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Local Supabase stack runtime state. `supabase start` writes container secrets here
# (supabase/.temp/start-secrets/**) — these must NEVER be committed. Migrations and
# config.toml are tracked; everything the running stack generates is not.
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/

# The control machinery in .claude IS product: agent contracts, the work skill, the phase
# files. It is TRACKED. A blanket ignore here once let five new phase files be committed
# silently as nothing while edits to their already-tracked siblings landed normally, so only
# these three - personal settings, runtime state, superseded tooling - stay ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/skills/prd-taskmaster/

# ai4good local tooling (not app code)
.codex_rate.html
_task_dump.txt
.taskmaster/state.json

.taskmaster/_premigration_backup/
.taskmaster/tasks/*.backup-*.json
.taskmaster/tasks/*.bak-*
loop/out/

# Local Supabase stack runtime state. `supabase start` writes container secrets here
# (supabase/.temp/start-secrets/**) — these must NEVER be committed. Migrations and
# config.toml are tracked; everything the running stack generates is not.
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/
